            <ArticleTitle>[Hormonal profile in chronic pain syndromes of somatogenic etiology].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The integral &quot;profile&quot; of the groups of inpatients suffering from somatogenic chronic painful syndromes was plotted on a material of a comprehensive study into central and peripheral hormones, the total content, and correlations. Enkephalins are shown to play the integrating part in the development of stress-algogenic reactions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
